  "title": "Supplementary Table S10. Longitudinal ΔBAA analysis",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. ΔBAA was calculated as BAA in 2015 minus BAA in 2011. Models were fitted by inverse-probability-weighted linear regression with robust standard errors, adjusting for the main covariate set and baseline phenotypic age. Coefficients describe associations of sustained exposure-pattern summaries with the BAA difference between waves; this supportive analysis does not estimate an individual within-person ageing change. The single-exposure O₃ rows at the 1-km and 500-m scales are identical by construction: because O₃ concentration surfaces are spatially smooth, the exposure-pattern classifications coincide across buffer scales, so the two rows are not independent replications.",
    "Abbreviations: BAA, biological age acceleration; CI, confidence interval; EVI, enhanced vegetation index; O₃, ozone."
  ],
